# Stable name for the loopback node the CamX bridge feeds.
#
# Matched on the card label rather than the device number: v4l2loopback is
# loaded with video_nr=-1 because fixed numbers collide with the iris and CamX
# nodes, so /dev/videoN is not predictable across boots or module loads.
#
# Pin ID_V4L_CAPABILITIES to capture for this one purpose-built node. With
# exclusive_caps=1, the kernel correctly reports OUTPUT during the module's
# original add event because camx-v4l2-bridge has not opened its producer side
# yet. 60-persistent-v4l.rules consequently stores ":video_output:" in udev's
# database. The node later changes to Video Capture, and a fresh v4l_id reports
# ":capture:", but the kernel capability transition emits no uevent; a desktop
# WirePlumber starting afterwards consumes the stale database value and creates
# a V4L Device without a Video/Source.
#
# This override is safe only because the card-label match identifies the
# package-owned bridge endpoint: it is never intended to be an OUTPUT device
# for desktop clients. The service separately waits for a dequeuable frame
# before display-manager starts, so publishing the endpoint's intended role
# here does not expose an unready camera to the graphical session.
SUBSYSTEM=="video4linux", ATTR{name}=="Tachyon CamX Bridge", \
    ENV{ID_V4L_CAPABILITIES}=":capture:", SYMLINK+="tachyon-camera"
